HOW COMPONENTS REACH A USER
===========================

Everything under src/, scripts/, tests/, docs/ and notebooks/ is the work of
the mosaic authors unless a module docstring says otherwise. Mosaic ships no
trained model weights.

  incorporated   Third-party source inside src/, adapted or verbatim. It
                 ships in the wheel.

  invoked        A separate program mosaic starts and talks to over a pipe,
                 a socket or the filesystem. Mosaic does not link, import or
                 ship it; the user installs it.

  read           A file format mosaic reads or writes without importing,
                 shipping or starting the program that produces it.

  optional       A distribution named in an optional extra. Installing
                 mosaic-behavior does not install it.

  fetched        Model weights downloaded from a hub at first use. Nothing
                 is fetched at install time and nothing is redistributed
                 here.

  implemented    A method mosaic carries out in its own code from a
                 published description. No upstream code is used.

Three components carry restrictions the AGPL does not. keypoint-MoSeq
prohibits commercial use. TRex requires a paid license for company use. The
MegaDescriptor identity weights, which a user may name but mosaic never
selects, are CC-BY-NC-4.0: they prohibit commercial use and require
attribution. All three are stated in full below.


